WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.120
Eleven tests passed against
a live partition service,

2
00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.560
run from a laptop.

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.960
Not any suite. The one built from
the commit this environment runs.

4
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:14.360
Here's how it knows, and what a
pass does and doesn't tell you.

5
00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:23.716
Fieldnote twelve.

6
00:00:23.716 --> 00:00:25.246
Prove it from your desk.

7
00:00:26.098 --> 00:00:28.068
How do you prove a service from your desk?

8
00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:33.028
spi test runs the suite the
deployed commit shipped,

9
00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:34.628
against your environment.

10
00:00:35.018 --> 00:00:38.228
--report shows what its tests prove.

11
00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:42.858
And a change on your machine reaches the
environment as a pin you can test the same

12
00:00:42.858 --> 00:00:43.428
way.

13
00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:50.810
When spi up resolved partition, it also
recorded the digest of the acceptance image

14
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.580
built from the same commit.

15
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.140
spi test reads that pair.

16
00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.620
It checks the environment is Deployable
and the service isn't borrowed,

17
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.850
fetches the commit's own descriptor,
resolver and verdict script,

18
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:07.780
mints the test callers, and
runs the image by digest.

19
00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.860
The report names the commit:

20
00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.980
the one spi info showed for partition.

21
00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:17.632
The verdict is the commit's own script:

22
00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:22.592
a zero exit, at least one test
that ran, and no failures.

23
00:01:22.822 --> 00:01:27.232
Here, twelve ran, eleven
passed, one was skipped.

24
00:01:28.022 --> 00:01:31.312
But JUnit counts an empty test as a pass.

25
00:01:32.182 --> 00:01:35.152
--report counts those,
and here there were none.

26
00:01:35.942 --> 00:01:37.872
--review goes further:

27
00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:42.822
a reviewer reads the suite's sources
against the service's own API docs,

28
00:01:42.822 --> 00:01:45.472
and grades what each test proves.

29
00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:51.466
To prove a change before a pull request,
build it into the environment's own

30
00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:57.186
registry. spi service pin --source
builds the JAR on your machine and the

31
00:01:57.186 --> 00:02:00.586
image in the environment's
ACR, pins it by digest,

32
00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:01.876
and waits for the rollout.

33
00:02:02.186 --> 00:02:06.746
Then spi test --source runs
your checkout's suite,

34
00:02:06.746 --> 00:02:10.756
labeled matched when its commit
and a clean tree equal the pin.

35
00:02:10.906 --> 00:02:12.996
Reset puts the canonical back.

36
00:02:15.446 --> 00:02:17.056
Follow one paired run.

37
00:02:17.126 --> 00:02:18.496
The guards pass:

38
00:02:18.646 --> 00:02:20.656
Deployable, not borrowed.

39
00:02:21.046 --> 00:02:24.096
The lock gives the commit
and the acceptance digest.

40
00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:26.966
GitHub, at that commit,
gives the descriptor,

41
00:02:26.966 --> 00:02:29.376
the resolver and the verdict script.

42
00:02:29.526 --> 00:02:33.526
The image runs by digest, as linux/amd64.

43
00:02:33.526 --> 00:02:36.566
And the verdict, with its
page, is the commit's own:

44
00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:39.056
eleven passed, one skipped.

45
00:02:41.938 --> 00:02:43.058
An easy mistake:

46
00:02:43.058 --> 00:02:46.508
the suite passed, so every
test checked something.

47
00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:48.908
A pass only counts tests.

48
00:02:48.978 --> 00:02:52.498
The report's Hollow column counts
the passing tests that prove nothing:

49
00:02:52.498 --> 00:02:56.668
the empty ones, and the ones a
review graded as proving nothing.

50
00:02:56.898 --> 00:02:59.228
For this suite it reads zero.

51
00:02:59.538 --> 00:03:04.508
But this run was never reviewed, so
that zero only means no test was empty.

52
00:03:04.658 --> 00:03:06.268
The scoreboard says so.

53
00:03:06.658 --> 00:03:12.428
Before you call a service proven, run
every suite with --report and --review.

54
00:03:15.102 --> 00:03:16.352
So now you can say:

55
00:03:16.582 --> 00:03:20.432
spi test runs the suite the
deployed commit shipped.

56
00:03:20.822 --> 00:03:25.712
A pass counts tests, and the
report shows what they prove.

57
00:03:26.102 --> 00:03:30.032
And a change on your desk
reaches the stack as a local pin.

58
00:03:32.288 --> 00:03:33.358
That's the season:

59
00:03:33.358 --> 00:03:36.638
whose image runs, who is
asking, what it holds,

60
00:03:36.638 --> 00:03:40.088
who it acts for, and how to
prove it from your desk.

